  "reference_notes": "Compared mature spreading shrub habit and wild-type pinnate foliage photographs to current seeds 1/4/7 and the entire 36 sheet. Explicit woody stools and attached daughter shoots carry seven-leaflet pinnate leaves, producing a dense irregular crown with separated upper branches and no spherical clumps. Selected the spring vegetative phase before cream flower cymes open; summer berries are absent. Ornamental Black Lace reference photographs were inspected but their purple dissected foliage was explicitly excluded. Heights approximately 1.85-3.75 m. Small leaf serrations remain unresolved at 25 mm. Accepted as a leafy spring elder shrub source; source acceptance does not endorse variants.",
